Port of macos/Sources/MalachiMail/MessageView/InvitationDayStripView.swift;
GTK: none yet (docs/calendar.md §5.7, Cal.DayStripOf). The invitation
card's mini day strip: an axis over the working hours of the invitation's
day with its whole hours labelled underneath, the busy spans of the
visible calendars as grey blocks, and the invitation's own slot as a
dashed blue block with its time above it. Drawn in code on the canvas
(InvitationDayStripView.xaml.cs); everything drawn is geometry and the
application's own time strings. A screen reader reads the card's clock
and conflict lines instead, so the strip is no element of its own.
-->
<UserControl
    x:Class="Malachi.App.Reader.InvitationDayStripView"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"
    IsTabStop="False"
    Visibility="Collapsed">
    <Canvas
        x:Name="Surface"
        HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
        SizeChanged="OnSizeChanged" />
</UserControl>
